// `signal`/`computed`/`effect` are `use std.reactive` imports, not prelude names (prelude-redesign
// P2a). Both forms work: a selective import binds the bare name; a whole-module import gives the
// qualified call (`reactive.signal(...)` intercepts ahead of registry dispatch — the builtins need
// the reactive graph, which the registry seam cannot reach). Ungated bare use is E0005 (see
// diagnostics/reactive_unimported.noe).
// expect: stdout "10"
// expect: stdout "3"
// expect: exit 0
use std.reactive.{signal, computed}
use std.{reactive}

count = signal(5)
doubled = computed(fn() => count.get() * 2)
echo doubled.get()

qualified = reactive.signal(3)
echo qualified.get()
